{
  "activity_uuid": "activity_4c973d5d-abb8-52c4-a038-0d14678c0d40",
  "name": "13.1 Fractions, equivalent forms and mixed numbers",
  "activity_type": "TYPE_DYNAMIC",
  "activity_sub_type": "SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fractions, equivalent forms and mixed numbers"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Learning objective: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Recognise proper and improper fractions, create equivalent fractions and convert mixed numbers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Understand the concept"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A fraction a/b represents a equal parts when a whole is divided into b equal parts, where b is nonzero. A positive proper fraction has numerator smaller than denominator. An improper fraction has numerator at least as large as its denominator."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Multiply or divide numerator and denominator by the same nonzero factor to obtain an equivalent fraction. To convert a positive mixed number w a/b to an improper fraction, use (wb+a)/b. To convert back, divide numerator by denominator: quotient is the whole part, remainder is the new numerator."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockImage",
        "attrs": {
          "blockObject": {
            "block_uuid": "block_a54648e7-ad11-5580-8182-23e576dc0194",
            "content": {
              "file_id": "2b298294-ff88-5ddc-b865-cc9414ebed54",
              "file_format": "png",
              "activity_uuid": "activity_4c973d5d-abb8-52c4-a038-0d14678c0d40"
            }
          },
          "size": {
            "width": 900
          },
          "alignment": "center",
          "unsplash_url": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_name": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_url": null,
          "unsplash_photo_url": null
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Three coloured cells out of eight equal cells represent 3/8."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Convert 3 2/7 into an improper fraction."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "(3×7+2)/7 = 23/7."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Convert 29/6 to a mixed number."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "29 ÷ 6 = 4 remainder 5, giving 4 5/6."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
